When building my portfolio site, the part I wanted to really understand was the 'Deployment' process. At first, I just thought of it as a magic button that puts my code on the internet. But I had my AI tutor break it down for me.

Here’s how I understand it now: When I write code in VS Code, those files only exist on my hard drive. Nobody else can see them. 'Deploying' (like using Vercel or Cloudflare) is basically copying my local files and handing them over to massive, super-fast computers (servers) that never turn off and are always connected to the internet. Now, when someone types my URL into their browser, the internet directs them to those always-awake servers, which immediately send back my HTML and CSS files to the visitor's screen. So, deployment isn't magic; it's just moving your files from a sleeping laptop to an always-awake global computer.
